From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:52:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: drd: allow userspace control of the role switch

Every other dual-role controller driver in the tree (dwc2, cdns3, mtu3,
musb, chipidea, renesas_usb3, intel-xhci, even dwc3-rtk) sets
allow_userspace_control; dwc3 is the only one that does not, which
leaves the role sysfs attribute invisible and makes the switch
impossible to drive for debugging or for products whose role manager
lives in userspace.

Set it, matching the rest of the tree.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
index 797786093..f202cffec 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
@@ -513,6 +513,7 @@ static int dwc3_setup_role_switch(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 	dwc3_role_switch.fwnode = dev_fwnode(dwc->dev);
 	dwc3_role_switch.set = dwc3_usb_role_switch_set;
 	dwc3_role_switch.get = dwc3_usb_role_switch_get;
+	dwc3_role_switch.allow_userspace_control = true;
 	dwc3_role_switch.driver_data = dwc;
 	dwc->role_sw = usb_role_switch_register(dwc->dev, &dwc3_role_switch);
 	if (IS_ERR(dwc->role_sw))
